# 15 — THE FIVE-DESTINATION VISUAL DIFFERENTIATION TEST

Before accepting the immersive experience, inspect at least five different destination journeys.

For each, record:

* Starting camera position.
* Travel path.
* Tunnel or transition identity.
* Arrival movement.
* Environment silhouette.
* Dominant material language.
* Lighting character.
* Primary interaction.
* Exit choreography.

Compare the results.

If several destinations have essentially the same environment with different labels, redesign them.

If every destination uses the same tunnel and identical camera movement, introduce meaningful destination-specific variations.

If a destination could be removed without losing any spatial identity or useful interaction, it needs further design.

**The objective is a shared universe containing distinct places, not one scene copied repeatedly.**

